{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-3859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}-2x<8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-3859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x & <8 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x-8 & <0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y={x}^{2}-2x-8$ lies below the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-2x-8 & =0 \\\\ (x+2)(x-4) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-2$ and $x=4,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/83e87f616c1e9a74065016df2d6a0bbfac5bcdc8ee9326721b13a2bd8a8f16d4.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-2x-8<0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is below the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-2<x<4.$ \n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in (-2,4).$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-3859" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bcb7ddd4ff13edf2acc1931d5a156aefd00349a5618144c262017127ac301db"} {"question" "q-3859" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-3859" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-2,4)"] ["math" "x\\in (-4,2)"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-2)\\cup (4,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,2)\\cup (8,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (2,8)"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-3859" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\in (-2,4)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-3952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of $-6{x}^{2}>-3x.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-3952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{x}^{2} & >-3x \\\\ -6{x}^{2}+3x & >0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-6{x}^{2}+3x$ lies above the $x$-axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-6{x}^{2}+3x & =0 \\\\ -3x(2x-1) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=\\frac{1}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/3dff64c74abd4981c69686cbbf7d79fdd49c7a7fde3bb266b2b6e11c441bcf20.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-6{x}^{2}+3x>0,\n$$\n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is above the $x$-axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0<x<\\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-3952" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bcb7ddd4ff13edf2acc1931d5a156aefd00349a5618144c262017127ac301db"} {"question" "q-3952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-3952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}<x<0"] ["math" "-\\frac{1}{2}<x<2"] ["math" "0<x<\\frac{1}{2}"] ["text" "$x<-\\frac{1}{2}$ or $x>0$"] ["text" "$x<0$ or $x>2$"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-3952" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0<x<\\frac{1}{2}"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of ${x}^{2}-8x<0.$\n\n{{field-1}} $<x$\n{{field-2}}{{field-3}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve the inequality \n\n$$\n{x}^{2}-8x<0,\n$$\n\nwe need to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola \n\n$$\ny={x}^{2}-8x\n$$\n\nlies *below* the $x$-axis.\n\nFirst, let's find the roots of the parabola:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-8x & =0 \\\\ x(x-8) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the roots are $x=0$ and $x=8,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/8c4acb1db29c8479f946d6d047fe79d9a87d7162de1ff0725e59052f93df85ce.png)\n\nThe values marked in blue show all $x$-values where the parabola lies *below* the axis. \n\nSo, the solution to the inequality is $0<x<8.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276402" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bcb7ddd4ff13edf2acc1931d5a156aefd00349a5618144c262017127ac301db"} {"question" "q-276402" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276402" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276402" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276402" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "<"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276402" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276402" "field" "field-3" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "8"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find the solution of $x+3\\ge 2{x}^{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the numbers to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x+3 & \\ge 2{x}^{2} \\\\ -2{x}^{2}+x+3 & \\ge 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=-2{x}^{2}+x+3$ lies **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2{x}^{2}+x+3 & =0 \\\\ 2{x}^{2}-x-3 & =0 \\\\ (2{x}^{2}-3x)+(2x-3) & =0 \\\\ x(2x-3)+(2x-3) & =0 \\\\ (x+1)(2x-3) & =0 \\\\ 2(x+1)(x-\\frac{3}{2}) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=-1$ and $x=\\frac{3}{2},$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/86d7fbea75961bdb83c014ca9febb735e6a1745f71e8e094de416998b2072630.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n-2{x}^{2}+x+3\\ge 0,\n$$\n\n \nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **above** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $-1\\le x\\le \\frac{3}{2}.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [-1,\\frac{3}{2}].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276407" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/hard "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bcb7ddd4ff13edf2acc1931d5a156aefd00349a5618144c262017127ac301db"} {"question" "q-276407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-1]\\cup [\\frac{3}{2},\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in (-\\infty ,-\\frac{3}{2}]\\cup [1,\\infty )"] ["math" "x\\in [-1,\\frac{3}{2}]"] ["math" "x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},1]"] ["math" "x\\in [-\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{3}{2}]"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276407" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\in [-1,\\frac{3}{2}]"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $4{x}^{2}\\le 12x$ and express the solution set in interval notation.\n\n$x\\in [${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$]$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To solve this inequality using the graphical method, we first need to move all of the terms to the left-hand side so that the right-hand side is $0.$ \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2} & \\le 12x \\\\ 4{x}^{2}-12x & \\le 0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we want to find the values of $x$ for which the parabola $y=4{x}^{2}-12x$ lies **below** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. Let's find the roots of the parabola by factoring:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}-12x & =0 \\\\ 4x(x-3) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe see that the roots are $x=0$ and $x=3,$ and we can graph the parabola as follows:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/assets/d81805f304bd45ddd595bd251202226d2b1ced494fe7816d0bc9f17ee8f998a0.png)\n\nSince we are interested in solving \n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}-12x\\le 0,\n$$\n\n \n\nwe look for the part of the parabola that is **below** the $x$-axis or touches this axis. \n\nBased on the graph, the solution is $0\\le x\\le 3.$\n\nUsing interval notation, we write $x\\in [0,3].$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276408" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "4bcb7ddd4ff13edf2acc1931d5a156aefd00349a5618144c262017127ac301db"} {"question" "q-276408" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276408" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "0"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336f3fa2"} {"question" "q-276408" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14029391/state.json" "file_sha256" "a7d3dea7ea4b363ddd98895049ee167871d3cebce78fd065de3f50ec336